    "summary": "Epic impact: covers Story s1 -- s1 built and landed sc1/sc2 matching their HLD interfaceSketches exactly, leaving s2's own contract (sc3) as a placeholder. This Task adds buildArgv's mode:'read-only' branch (emits exactly the two connector_insrc_* --enabled-tools flags, never an approval flag regardless of request.approval) and stableDescriptorHash (resolved binary content identity via path+size+mtime, buildArgv's own argv with --output-dir excluded, the adapter's pinned env subset, and cwd). Added a test-only export, _buildArgvForTests, so tests can observe buildArgv's real output directly (buildArgv itself stays unexported in production, consistent with the module's existing test-seam pattern such as _readOnlyQualificationCacheForTests). Left out: resolving the binary via a full content hash (read+hash the whole binary) rather than path+size+mtime -- the lighter stat-based identity avoids re-hashing a potentially large binary on every read-only dispatch while still changing on any install/upgrade; this is a design judgment call disclosed here, not hidden.",
